    summary: `# 🦠 Zoonoses #5 — Protozoal Zoonoses

## 🎯 Major protozoal zoonoses

| Disease | Pathogen | Reservoir | Transmission |
|---|---|---|---|
| Toxoplasmosis | *Toxoplasma gondii* | Cats (definitive) | Oocysts, undercooked meat |
| Cryptosporidiosis | *Cryptosporidium parvum* | Calves | Water, fecal-oral |
| Giardiasis | *Giardia duodenalis* | Beavers, dogs | Water |
| Amebiasis | *Entamoeba histolytica* | Human (mostly) | Fecal-oral |
| Leishmaniasis | *Leishmania* spp. | Dogs, rodents | Sand fly |
| Trypanosomiasis | *Trypanosoma* spp. | Cattle, wild | Tsetse, kissing bug |
| Babesiosis | *Babesia* spp. | Cattle, deer | Tick |

## 🐱 Toxoplasmosis (most important!)

### Life cycle
- **Definitive host:** cats — sexual cycle in intestine
- **Intermediate hosts:** all warm-blooded animals (incl. humans)
- **Stages:** tachyzoite (acute), bradyzoite (cyst, latent), oocyst (cat feces)

### Transmission
- Cat oocysts (sporulated 1-5 days)
- Undercooked meat (bradyzoites in pork, lamb, venison)
- Vertical (transplacental)
- Organ transplant, blood transfusion (rare)

### Clinical
- **Immunocompetent:** asymptomatic or mild flu-like
- **Pregnant:** fetal infection (severe!) — chorioretinitis, hydrocephalus, calcifications
- **Immunocompromised (AIDS):** reactivation → encephalitis
- **Cats:** mostly asymptomatic, rarely uveitis/hepatic

### Diagnosis
- IgG/IgM serology (paired)
- PCR (CSF, amniotic fluid)
- Histopathology (cysts in tissue)

### Treatment
- Pyrimethamine + sulfadiazine + leucovorin
- Spiramycin (pregnancy)

### Prevention
- Cook meat thoroughly (>67°C, freezing -12°C 24h)
- Wash vegetables
- Wear gloves when gardening / cleaning litter box
- Don't feed cats raw meat

## 🐄 Cryptosporidiosis
- *C. parvum* — calves, lambs, kids
- Veterinary occupational hazard (calf diarrhea handlers!)
- Watery diarrhea, self-limiting (immunocompetent)
- Severe in AIDS (untreatable)
- Resistant to chlorine (water-borne outbreaks)

## 🐶 Leishmaniasis (Mediterranean, S. America)
- Sand fly vector
- Cutaneous + visceral forms
- Dog = major reservoir (visceral L. infantum)
- Thailand: rare, sporadic imported

## 🐄 Trypanosomiasis
- *T. brucei* (sleeping sickness, Africa) — tsetse fly
- *T. cruzi* (Chagas, Americas) — kissing bug
- *T. evansi* (Surra, Asia) — biting flies, livestock zoonotic risk

## 🩸 Babesiosis
- *B. microti* (USA), *B. divergens* (Europe)
- Tick vector (*Ixodes*)
- Cattle reservoir
- Hemolytic disease (like malaria)

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ Toxoplasmosis: cats definitive, pregnancy = high risk
2. ⭐ Tachyzoite (acute) vs bradyzoite (cyst, latent)
3. ⭐ Cryptosporidium = calf diarrhea handlers' risk
4. ⭐ Leishmaniasis = sand fly + dog reservoir
5. ⭐ Cook meat 67°C kills Toxo bradyzoites`,
